#doc (Manual) "To be formalised" =>

31 entries. Nothing formalised yet. Each entry says what blocks it: missing theory, a database numbering, or nothing but work.

# Fields › Local fields

* [`lf.family_varying`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Fields/Local-fields/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_lf___family_varying_FLQQ_--statement) — Data that varies within families. Difficulty: hard, theory. *Blocked by:* Example families in which each listed invariant varies (Galois group, hidden Artin slopes, indices of inseparability, associated inertia, jump set), which needs these invariants of explicit p-adic extensions, several of them not formalised.

# Groups › Abstract groups

* [`group.hash`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Groups/Abstract-groups/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_group___hash_FLQQ_--statement) — Hash for abstract groups. Difficulty: very hard, theory. *Blocked by:* The number of groups of order 512 up to isomorphism, 10,494,213 (Eick–O'Brien), which needs a verified enumeration of 2-groups. The hash and the LMFDB counts are database.

# Groups › Sato–Tate groups

* [`rcs.rigor.st_group`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Groups/Sato-Tate-groups/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_rcs___rigor___st_group_FLQQ_--statement) — Reliability of Sato-Tate Group Data. Difficulty: very hard, theory. *Blocked by:* The Sato–Tate axioms, Sato–Tate groups of abelian surfaces, and the Fité–Kedlaya–Rotger–Sutherland classification (55 groups satisfying the axioms in weight 1 and degree 4, 52 of them occurring). LeanBridge has 'SatoTateGroup' and 'SatoTateGroup.IsRational'.

# L-functions

* [`intro.features`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/L-functions/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_intro___features_FLQQ_--statement) — Introduction/Features. Difficulty: very hard, information. *Blocked by:* The belief that the lowest zero above the real axis determines the L-function must first be made precise: as stated it fails for imprimitive L-functions (a product L₁L₂ has the lower of its factors' lowest zeros); for primitive ones it is a folklore conjecture, open and stated nowhere. LeanBridge has the lowest zero, 'AnalyticLFunction.lowestZero'; the rest is site features.
* [`lfunction.history.hasse_weil`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/L-functions/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_lfunction___history___hasse_weil_FLQQ_--statement) — Hasse-Weil L-function. Difficulty: very hard, theory. *Blocked by:* Hasse's expression of the Hasse–Weil zeta function of the Fermat curve x\^m + y\^m = 1 through L-functions of (Jacobi-sum) Hecke characters: Hasse–Weil zeta functions of curves over number fields and Hecke L-functions are formalised nowhere (Tau Ceti has Hecke characters, Mathlib Jacobi sums).
* [`lfunction.history.rankin_selberg`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/L-functions/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_lfunction___history___rankin_selberg_FLQQ_--statement) — Ranking-Selberg convolution, history. Difficulty: very hard, theory. *Blocked by:* Rankin's theorem that ζ(2s − 22)g(s), with g(s) = Σ τ(n)² n\^(−s), is analytic except for a simple pole at s = 12 and has a functional equation: it needs the Rankin–Selberg unfolding against real-analytic Eisenstein series with their continuation, formalised nowhere. Δ and τ are in Mathlib and Tau Ceti.
* [`rcs.cande.lfunction`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/L-functions/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_rcs___cande___lfunction_FLQQ_--statement) — Completeness of L-function Data. Difficulty: very hard, theory. *Blocked by:* The counts it states: 1 741 002 isogeny classes over ℚ of conductor ≤ 400 000, 38 042 of them of conductor ≤ 10 000 matching weight-2 newforms (modularity; very hard), 51 cubic fields with \|D\| ≤ 368 (hard), 4296 quadratic fields with \|D\| ≤ 7071 (medium) and 1 448 484 primitive characters of conductor ≤ 2800 (easy to medium). The notions exist: Mathlib's 'DirichletCharacter.IsPrimitive' and 'Int.IsFundamentalDiscr', LeanBridge's 'WeierstrassCurve.IsModular'.
* [`rcs.cande.zeros.zeta`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/L-functions/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_rcs___cande___zeros___zeta_FLQQ_--statement) — Completeness of Riemann Zeta Zeros Data. Difficulty: very hard, theory. *Blocked by:* Platt's count of the 103,800,788,359 zeros of ζ with imaginary part in (0, 30 610 046 000\], all on the critical line: a certified computation of about 10¹¹ zeros. Mathlib has the zeros ('riemannZetaZeros', 'IsCompact.inter\_riemannZetaZeros\_finite') and RH as a statement ('RiemannHypothesis').
* [`rcs.rigor.lfunction.dirichlet`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/L-functions/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_rcs___rigor___lfunction___dirichlet_FLQQ_--statement) — Reliability of Dirichlet L-function Data. Difficulty: very hard, theory. *Blocked by:* Certified L(1/2, χ) ≠ 0 and low zeros on the critical line for the database's characters (all primitive characters of conductor ≤ 2800 among them). LeanBridge has the L-functions and the critical line ('AnalyticLFunction.dirichlet', 'AnalyticLFunction.criticalLine').
* [`rcs.rigor.lfunction.ec`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/L-functions/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_rcs___rigor___lfunction___ec_FLQQ_--statement) — Reliability of Elliptic Curve L-function Data. Difficulty: very hard, theory. *Blocked by:* That 234446.a1 has rank 4 (hard) and analytic rank 2 or 4 (modularity and certified numerics; very hard). LeanBridge has 'WeierstrassCurve.IsAnalyticLFunction'.

# Modular forms › Bianchi

* [`rcs.cande.mf.bianchi`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Modular-forms/Bianchi-modular-forms/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_rcs___cande___mf___bianchi_FLQQ_--statement) — Completeness of Bianchi modular form data. Difficulty: very hard, theory. *Blocked by:* That every imaginary quadratic field of class number ≤ 5 other than ℚ(√−2683) has \|D\| \< 2500 (the class number ≤ 5 problem; no tree has lower bounds for class numbers), and the count of 763 imaginary quadratic fields with \|D\| \< 2500 (medium). The notions are Mathlib's 'Int.IsFundamentalDiscr' and 'NumberField.classNumber'.

# Modular forms › Maass

* [`rcs.cande.maass_rigor`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Modular-forms/Maass-forms/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_rcs___cande___maass_rigor_FLQQ_--statement) — Completeness and extent of rigorous Maass form data. Difficulty: very hard, information. *Blocked by:* The conjecture must first be stated precisely: as written ('each piece of data … is conjecturally transcendental') it is false (a₁ = 1, and a\_p = ±p\^(−1/2) for p dividing a squarefree N), and dihedral forms have algebraic Hecke eigenvalues; the text needs a correction, recorded in the LMFDB issues, and the precise conjecture is open. The notions exist: LeanBridge's 'UpperHalfPlane.IsMaassCuspNewform' and Mathlib's 'Transcendental'.
* [`rcs.rigor.maass`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Modular-forms/Maass-forms/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_rcs___rigor___maass_FLQQ_--statement) — Reliability of Maass forms data. Difficulty: very hard, information. *Blocked by:* The conjecture must first be stated precisely: 'in general' must exclude, for instance, dihedral forms, whose Hecke eigenvalues are algebraic; the precise conjecture is open. The notions exist: LeanBridge's 'UpperHalfPlane.IsMaassCuspNewform' and Mathlib's 'Transcendental'.
* [`rcs.rigor.maass_rigor`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Modular-forms/Maass-forms/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_rcs___rigor___maass_rigor_FLQQ_--statement) — Reliability of rigorous Maass forms data. Difficulty: very hard, information. *Blocked by:* The conjecture must first be stated precisely: 'in general' must exclude, for instance, dihedral forms, whose Hecke eigenvalues are algebraic; the precise conjecture is open. The notions exist: LeanBridge's 'UpperHalfPlane.IsMaassCuspNewform' and Mathlib's 'Transcendental'.

# Modular forms › Miscellaneous

* [`mf.gl2.history.hecke`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Modular-forms/Modular-forms-miscellaneous/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_mf___gl2___history___hecke_FLQQ_--statement) — Hecke Characters. Difficulty: very hard, theory. *Blocked by:* Hecke's theorem that the forms of Hecke characters of quadratic fields are cusp forms, combinations of the theta series Θ\_\{L;Q;h\}; that they are exactly the CM forms (Ribet's converse); the lacunarity of CM forms, with the definition of lacunary; and Serre's lacunarity theorem, which needs the Galois representations of newforms. CM newforms and Hecke characters exist in LeanBridge ('HeckeRing.GL2.Newform.HasCM', 'TauCeti.GlobalNumberFields.IsIdealHeckeCharacter').

# Modular forms › Siegel

* [`mf.siegel.extent.kp`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Modular-forms/Siegel-modular-forms/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_mf___siegel___extent___kp_FLQQ_--statement) — Available samples for \$M\_2(K(p))\$. Difficulty: very hard, theory. *Blocked by:* Poor–Yuen's theorem that S₂(K(277)) contains a nonlift eigenform, and the nonlifts at levels 349, 353, 389, 461, 523 and 587 that the knowl calls conjectured. Nonlift newforms and Gritsenko lifts are defined in LeanBridge ('SiegelUpperHalfSpace.IsParamodularNonliftNewform', 'SiegelUpperHalfSpace.IsGritsenkoLift').
* [`mf.siegel.family.sp8z`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Modular-forms/Siegel-modular-forms/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_mf___siegel___family___sp8z_FLQQ_--statement) — The ring of Siegel modular forms of degree 4 with respect to the full modular group. Difficulty: very hard, theory. *Blocked by:* Poor–Yuen's dimensions of S\_k(Sp(8, ℤ)) for k ≤ 16, that every cusp form of weight ≤ 14 is a Duke–Imamoḡlu–Ikeda or Miyawaki lift, and Ibukiyama's weight-16 eigenforms of a conjectural lift; no lift of degree 4 is defined. Degree-4 Siegel cusp forms can be defined with LeanBridge's 'SiegelUpperHalfSpace.siegelCuspForms'.

# Varieties › Abelian varieties over 𝔽\_q

* [`av.fq.class_number_1`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Varieties/Abelian-varieties-over-Fq/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_av___fq___class_number_1_FLQQ_--statement) — Function fields of class number 1. Difficulty: very hard, theory. *Blocked by:* The classification (Leitzel–Madan–Queen, Stirpe, Mercuri–Stirpe, Shen–Shi): up to isomorphism exactly 8 function fields of positive genus over finite fields have class number 1, which needs the Riemann hypothesis for curves of genus up to 4 (Tau Ceti main has only Hasse's bound for elliptic curves) and a finite search; only the class number exists (Tau Ceti's 'TauCeti.Divisor.classNumber'). The text needs a correction ('of positive genus': every genus-0 curve has class number 1), recorded in the LMFDB issues.
* [`av.fq.one_rational_point`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Varieties/Abelian-varieties-over-Fq/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_av___fq___one_rational_point_FLQQ_--statement) — Abelian varieties with one rational point. Difficulty: very hard, theory. *Blocked by:* The Madan–Pal classification up to isogeny of the simple abelian varieties over finite fields with one rational point, which needs the Weil polynomials of abelian varieties and Honda–Tate theory (av.fq.honda\_tate); the explicit family of Weil polynomials alone is medium. LeanBridge has only the notions: 'Polynomial.IsWeilPolynomial', 'Polynomial.IsHondaTate' and 'TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.AbelianVariety.HasWeilPolynomial'.
* [`rcs.source.av.fq`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Varieties/Abelian-varieties-over-Fq/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_rcs___source___av___fq_FLQQ_--statement) — Source of isogeny classes of abelian varieties over finite fields. Difficulty: very hard, theory. *Blocked by:* Tate's isogeny theorem over finite fields (isogeny classes are determined by the characteristic polynomial of Frobenius); the place-count constraint is trivial for actual counts, and its content (counts from the Weil polynomial) needs the rationality of the zeta function. LeanBridge has 'TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.AbelianVariety.HasWeilPolynomial' and 'TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.AbelianVariety.IsIsogenous'.

# Varieties › Elliptic curves

* [`dq.ecnf.reliability`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Varieties/Elliptic-curves/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_dq___ecnf___reliability_FLQQ_--statement) — Reliability of elliptic curve data over number fields. Difficulty: very hard, theory. *Blocked by:* Modularity of elliptic curves over totally real fields of degree 2 and 3 and (Box) most of degree 4, and that modular elliptic curves satisfy the Hasse–Weil conjecture; no tree has modularity over number fields (LeanBridge's 'WeierstrassCurve.IsModular' is over ℚ only). The rest is about the reliability of the data.
* [`rcs.cande.ec`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Varieties/Elliptic-curves/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_rcs___cande___ec_FLQQ_--statement) — Completeness of elliptic curve data. Difficulty: very hard, theory. *Blocked by:* Modularity of elliptic curves over real quadratic and totally real cubic fields; LeanBridge's 'WeierstrassCurve.IsModular' is over ℚ only.
* [`rcs.rigor.ec.q`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Varieties/Elliptic-curves/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_rcs___rigor___ec___q_FLQQ_--statement) — Reliability of elliptic curve data over \$\\Q\$. Difficulty: very hard, theory. *Blocked by:* The modularity theorem with level equal to the conductor (Wiles, Breuil–Conrad–Diamond–Taylor, Carayol), Gross–Zagier–Kolyvagin (r = r\_an when r\_an ≤ 1), Mazur's torsion theorem, and L(E, 1)/Ω ∈ ℚ\_\{\>0\} in rank 0 (Manin–Drinfeld). LeanBridge states modularity as 'WeierstrassCurve.IsModular'.

# Varieties › Genus 2 curves

* [`rcs.rigor.g2c`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Varieties/Genus-2-curves/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_rcs___rigor___g2c_FLQQ_--statement) — Reliability of Genus 2 Curve Data. Difficulty: very hard, theory. *Blocked by:* L-functions of abelian surfaces, hence 'Hasse–Weil implies Selberg class' and the Hasse–Weil conjecture for Jacobians of GL₂-type (Ribet with Khare–Wintenberger). LeanBridge has the Selberg class, 'LSeries.selbergClass'.

# Varieties › Modular curves

* [`modcurve.known_points`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Varieties/Modular-curves/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_modcurve___known_points_FLQQ_--statement) — Known points. Difficulty: very hard, theory. *Blocked by:* X\_H as a curve over ℚ with its j-map, for the split of its points into cusps, CM points and others and for the cusps lying over j = ∞ (as in modcurve.rational\_points and modcurve.cusps). The rest concerns the stored points and search.
* [`modcurve.x0.remarks`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Varieties/Modular-curves/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_modcurve___x0___remarks_FLQQ_--statement) — Remarks on \$X\_0(N)\$. Difficulty: very hard, theory. *Blocked by:* X₀(N) as a curve over ℚ, with the theorems of Ogg (19 hyperelliptic X₀(N)), Bars (41 bielliptic) and Mazur–Kenku (26 with non-cuspidal rational points), which needs Mazur's theorem. The link to the 30 non-hyperelliptic bielliptic levels needs a correction (102 for 101), recorded in the LMFDB issues.
* [`modcurve.x1.remarks`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Varieties/Modular-curves/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_modcurve___x1___remarks_FLQQ_--statement) — Remarks on \$X\_1(N)\$. Difficulty: very hard, theory. *Blocked by:* X₁(N) as a curve over ℚ, with the theorems of Ishii–Momose (3 hyperelliptic X₁(N)), Jeon–Kim (8 bielliptic) and Mazur's torsion theorem (non-cuspidal rational points exactly for the genus-0 levels N ≤ 10 and 12), beyond current libraries.
* [`modcurve.xsp.remarks`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Varieties/Modular-curves/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_modcurve___xsp___remarks_FLQQ_--statement) — Remarks on \$X\_\{\\mathrm\{sp\}\}(N)\$. Difficulty: very hard, theory. *Blocked by:* The curves X\_sp(N) and X₀(N²) over ℚ, for the isomorphism X\_sp(N) ≅ X₀(N²) (through τ ↦ Nτ) and the absence of hyperelliptic curves (no square in Ogg's list); LeanBridge has only the groups.
* [`modcurve.xsp_plus.remarks`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Varieties/Modular-curves/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_modcurve___xsp_plus___remarks_FLQQ_--statement) — Remarks on \$X\_\{\\mathrm\{sp\}\}\^+(N)\$. Difficulty: very hard, theory. *Blocked by:* The cited classification of the hyperelliptic X\_sp⁺(N) (only N = 11), a theorem on curves that are not formalised.

# Varieties › Shimura curves

* [`shimcurve.genus_minus_rank`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Varieties/Shimura-curves/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_shimcurve___genus_minus_rank_FLQQ_--statement) — Genus-rank difference. Difficulty: very hard, theory. *Blocked by:* The analytic rank of X\_H (shimcurve.rank): Shimura curves, their Jacobians and the L-functions of these Jacobians; the genus half is partly formalised (shimcurve.genus). Note: Attempted in the round of 30 October: Needs the Shimura curve X\_H as an algebraic curve (for the genus of a geometric component) and its analytic rank, the order of vanishing at the central point of the L-function of its Jacobian; neither Shimura curves nor their Jacobians and L-functions are available, and a bare difference of two given integers would be vacuous.
* [`shimcurve.rank`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Varieties/Shimura-curves/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_shimcurve___rank_FLQQ_--statement) — Analytic rank. Difficulty: very hard, theory. *Blocked by:* The L-function of the Jacobian of X\_H continued to the central point: Shimura curves, their Jacobians and the Jacquet–Langlands decomposition into modular abelian varieties of newforms. Note: Attempted in the round of 30 October: Needs the Jacobian of the Shimura curve X\_H and its L-function continued to the central point, or its Jacquet–Langlands decomposition into modular abelian varieties of newforms; Shimura curves, their Jacobians and these L-functions are not available.
